AB  - Innovative technologies with adequate implementation strategies are essential in Nigeria as Irrigation agriculture accounts for 70% of water use worldwide and irrigation farming in most nations of the World. This paper explores the crucial role of civil engineers in the deployment of innovative strategies and implementation of sustainable irrigation infrastructure in Nigeria. Irrigation systems are currently facing serious challenges due to growing scarcity and competition for water. The methodology includes literature reviews and case studies. Various innovative technologies and implementation strategies were highlighted for sustainable irrigation infrastructure in Nigeria. Remote sensing encompasses satellite imagery, aerial photography, and unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) to collect data on crop conditions, soil moisture, and water availability. It was discovered that the implementation of sustainable irrigation infrastructure is of paramount importance for Nigeria's agricultural development, food security, and overall economic growth. The significance of sustainable irrigation infrastructure, innovative technologies and strategies can be employed by civil engineers and other professionals to address these challenges. Civil engineers possess the expertise, knowledge, and skills to design, implement, and manage sustainable irrigation infrastructure projects. Technological innovations, policy and governance, financing and investment, case studies, and community engagement can be used to achieve sustainable irrigation infrastructure. © 2024 IEEE.
